Recovery order is a business decision disguised as a technical checklist.

Before testing a restore, define:
- the service being recovered;
- dependent identity, network, storage, and application components;
- the backup source and recovery location;
- the validation owner and success criteria;
- user communication and fallback steps;
- the result, gaps, and follow-up owner.

Cloud2e's managed IT service includes monitored backups and tested restores as part of ongoing operations. Combining recovery testing with transparent reporting helps leaders see what was tested, what worked, and what still needs attention. It does not promise an outage-free environment; it turns recovery from an assumption into an operational exercise.

Start with one business-critical service and build a repeatable recovery sequence around it.

